To give the current nasties some company.  (By the way, I also imagine
this patch would make the current demon lords and princes a bit
beefier, except for Demogorgon.)

>From Paradise Lost:

Belial: Would be physically weak compared to his comrades.  PL
represents him as being a kind of shifty lawyer sort, so it'd be nice
if a logic puzzle could be constructed around him, or maybe Sphinx-like
riddles.

Mammon: Would essentially be a super leprechaun.  Like leps, he would
have disproportionately-great hit points to make him difficult to
one-hit-kill, but relatively little attack strength.  Also like leps,
he would teleport randomly instead of to the upstairs.  Unlike leps,
the player could not outlevel him, and he would be interested in
stealing gemstones too (not glass: he'd know the difference) and maybe
even magic items with gemstone or valuable metal descriptions, and
could even steal valuable objects from out of bags.  He would not have
an interest in the Amulet, bell, book, candle or artifacts though.
Mammon would not have a tremendous grudge against the player: acquiring
wealth is his main goal, but it would cost a lot of gold to pay him
off.

>From other sources:
Lucifer: In the old game UltraRogue, formerly one of Hack's competitors
but has long since fallen into obscurity, Lucifer was the main
opponent, who, after the player had obtained one of the game-win
artifacts and made it back to the top level, would be waiting for the
player by the upstairs.  That seems a cool idea to me, and seeing as
how UltraRogue is almost forgotten now and good ideas shouldn't go to
waste, maybe he should be resurrected in Nethack?  What do you guys
think?

On the instant controlled teleport trick:
I think it's little too predictable for some of these guys, it'd be
nice to see, if the player is standing on the stairs, them do random
teleports (though less frequently than the controlled 'port, so it
doesn't get too hard for the player) instead of just standing around.
It may be good to give the port-at-will monsters a Power score that
'porting would take points from, so an outclassed monster won't end up
fleeing forever but would eventually run out of magic.  (It'd also
perhaps give a use to a wand that drained magic, but that would be a
separate YANI.)

